prompts.prompt:
Assess the document text below. State: what type of document it appears to be, which of the expected fields are present, which are missing, and any internal inconsistency (dates that cannot both be true, totals that do not add up, names that differ between sections). Report only what the text supports. You are not authenticating the document — do not state that it is genuine or forged.

Every factual or regulatory claim MUST end with a citation in the exact form [Source: <title>|<url>], pointing at official regulator material. If you cannot cite an official source for a claim, omit the claim. If you can cite nothing at all, reply only with: I don't have a verified source for this.

Expected fields: {{FIELDS}}

Document text:
{{INPUT}}

Extract the requested fields from the document text and return ONLY a JSON object whose keys are exactly the requested field names. Use null for any field the text does not contain — never guess, never infer a value from a similar field, and never return a partially-read number. Dates as YYYY-MM-DD. Do not wrap the JSON in prose or code fences.

Requested fields: {{FIELDS}}

Document text:
{{INPUT}}

The submitted form data failed one or more validation rules. For each failure, explain in one sentence what is wrong and what the person should change, addressed to them, in plain language and without jargon. Do not invent rules that are not in the list.

Rules:
{{VALIDATIONRULES}}

Submitted data:
{{INPUT}}

Given the case state and the available transitions, recommend which transition to take and why, in at most three sentences. Recommend only from the transitions listed. If the state does not justify any of them, say so and say what is missing. You are advising a human who decides — do not phrase this as an instruction or imply the transition has happened.

Every factual or regulatory claim MUST end with a citation in the exact form [Source: <title>|<url>], pointing at official regulator material. If you cannot cite an official source for a claim, omit the claim. If you can cite nothing at all, reply only with: I don't have a verified source for this.

Case state:
{{INPUT}}

Available transitions: {{TRANSITIONS}}

Assess how the regulatory change below affects the obligation described. State: whether the obligation's requirement, deadline or evidence changes; what specifically changes; and what the institution must do differently. If the change does not affect this obligation, say so plainly rather than manufacturing a connection.

Every factual or regulatory claim MUST end with a citation in the exact form [Source: <title>|<url>], pointing at official regulator material. If you cannot cite an official source for a claim, omit the claim. If you can cite nothing at all, reply only with: I don't have a verified source for this.

Obligation:
{{CONTEXT}}

Regulatory change:
{{INPUT}}

